Package: noisyvalue
Title: Tidy R Interface to the Python noisyvalue Library
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Steven", "Baldasty", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Thin reticulate-based wrappers around the Python noisyvalue
    library. Exposes NoisyValue-backed pandas DataFrame columns as
    tibble-compatible R vectors, and forwards R arithmetic and comparison
    operators straight through to the underlying Python objects so that
    posterior/symbolic provenance is preserved through R code.
License: MIT
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    reticulate,
    tibble,
    vctrs
Suggests:
    dplyr,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
